Description: Estimation of hierarchical spatio-temporal models through the
    Expectation-Maximization (EM) algorithm within a likelihood-based
    framework, following Fasso and Cameletti (2010)
    <doi:10.1177/0037549709102150> and the heterogeneous-network model of
    Fasso, Cameletti and Nicolis (2007) <doi:10.1002/env.837>, with the EM
    machinery of McLachlan and
    Krishnan (2008, ISBN:9780470191613). Parameters are estimated by maximum
    likelihood via Kalman filtering and smoothing; standard errors and spatial
    prediction uncertainty are obtained by a spatio-temporal parametric
    bootstrap. The package also provides the spatially-clustered STEM (SC-STEM)
    models, an extension in which regression coefficients, variance components
    and latent dynamics vary across spatial regimes estimated from the data by
    maximising a Potts-penalised likelihood, in the spirit of the
    spatially-clustered regression of Sugasawa and Murakami (2021)
    <doi:10.1016/j.spasta.2021.100525> and of the spatially-clustered spatial
    autoregressive models of Cerqueti, Maranzano and Mattera (2025)
    <doi:10.1007/s13253-025-00685-7>. SC-STEM comes with likelihood-based
    criteria and a stability-based rule for selecting the number of clusters
    and the spatial penalty, and with a refit-with-clustering parametric
    bootstrap that propagates the uncertainty of the estimated partition.
